Requirements:
- Compare at least one control condition (is_baseline = true) with the treatment condition(s); short snake_case names.
- Name the unit of analysis (unit_of_analysis): the independent unit that is assigned to a condition and measured, such as a participant, patient, animal, plot or sample. Repeated measurements of one unit (visits, cells, technical replicates) are not independent units.
- Mark exactly one metric as the primary outcome (primary = true), fixed before any data exist, and say for every metric which way is better.
- Statistics: name "Welch t-test" or "Mann-Whitney U" if each unit is in one condition, "paired t-test" or "Wilcoxon signed-rank" if every unit is measured under every condition.
- expected_effect_size: Cohen's d of the smallest effect on the primary metric that would matter; rtool computes the sample size from it.
- List the materials and say who is blinded. Write the procedure as steps a person in a lab or in the field can follow, ending with recording one row per unit and condition.
- n_seeds is ignored: units are the repetitions.
